      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-135412",
      ":question/problem": "A study determines how customers' yearly preferences change between the LB and SB telephone companies. The table below describes the results of this study.\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **LB** | **SB** |\n| To: | **LB** | $0$ | $0.25$ |\n| **SB** | $1$ | $0.75$ |  |\n\nIt's found that $100%$ of the customers who currently use the LB company will choose the SB company next year, while $25%$ of the customers who currently use the SB company will use the LB company next year.\n\nAssuming that there are $100\\,000$ customers in total and that the given probabilities remain constant over many years, determine the number of customers who will eventually use the SB company."
    }
  ],
